Sir, **ApexForm** is a complete, production-ready Android application built in **Kotlin** using **Jetpack Compose**, **Material 3**, **MVVM**, and **Room Database**. It is engineered specifically for gym athletes, calisthenics practitioners, and gymnasts to solve daily training, progressive overload, supplement timing, hydration, and macro tracking in one unified offline-first interface.

---

## 1. Architecture & Core Modules

* **Tech Stack:** Kotlin, Jetpack Compose (Material 3), Coroutines & `StateFlow`, Room (SQLite local persistence), ViewModel.
* **Solved Pain Points:**
* **Workout & Skill Progression:** Tracks both weighted gym lifts (sets/reps/kg) and gymnastic isometric holds (seconds), complete with an integrated countdown rest timer.
* **Supplement Routine Engine:** Organizes supplements by timing window (Morning, Pre-Workout, Post-Workout, Before Bed) with dosage tracking and daily reset checklists.
* **Hydration & Macro Dashboard:** One-tap water logging (+250 ml) and live calorie/protein progress rings.



